  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A liquid having a coefficient of volume expansion&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>γ</mi></math>&nbsp;is filled in a cylindrical vessel made out of glass having coefficient of linear expansion&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>. At room temperature, the level of liquid in the vessel is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and when the temperature is increased by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></math>, the level of liquid in the vessel becomes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>? [Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></math>]&nbsp;</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let us assume that the volume of the liquid in the vessel is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and the area of cross-section of the vessel is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>, then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Similarly,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Using binomial approximation, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Neglecting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi><mi>γ</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, since it is insignificant as compared to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></math>,&nbsp;we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>α</mi><mo>∆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
